**Dev GPU box (2026-09-18):** `i-00da21ca8277ecd1d`, account 368351959688, role `taiboli-dev-hd-instance-profile-gpu-server-role`, region ap-south-2, public IP 16.113.55.93, key `~/.ssh/taiboli-non-prod-gpu`. Serving container `musetalk` (`:dev`, host network, port 8000, mounts `/opt/models` + `/opt/musetalk-data/video`, NO NVMe mount). Cloudflare tunnel routes `dev-avatar.taiboli.in` → 8000 only. This is NOT the prod box from earlier sessions (account 985..., NVMe avatar cache shared with prod).

**Parallel perf run:** `sudo /opt/gpu-server/scripts/fetch-env.sh` (SSM → `/run/avatar.env`, root 0600, tmpfs) then `./perf_check.sh <ecr>/musetalk:perf-<slug>[-<sha7>]` with no flags. After the 2026-09-18 fix the defaults are right for these boxes: env via sudo copy, models `/opt/models`, own cache `/opt/dlami/nvme/perf-avatar-cache`, quality store `/opt/dlami/nvme/quality`, port 8001 (bridge, `-p 8001:8000`). Browser test needs `ssh -i ~/.ssh/taiboli-non-prod-gpu -L 8001:localhost:8001 ubuntu@<ip>` then `http://localhost:8001/`. Cross-account ECR pull to 755348349838 works with the instance role; `ecr:DescribeImages/ListImages` does not (use `docker manifest inspect` to check a tag).

**Measured 2026-09-18 on `perf-s3-avatar-cache` @ 4a96788:** avatar cache 5.9 GB from S3 in 8 s (only core files + `runtime/*.npy`, no `full_imgs`/`mask` — that is what the branch's `_cache_exists` change enables); listening 29 s, fully warmed 33 s; warm restart 20 s. Two containers idle at ~3.2 GB GPU each, ~5 GB after a session. Quality baseline for `avator_1` recorded in the local store (not mirrored to S3 yet); in-process noise floor bit-identical, cross-process min face PSNR 68.5 dB → PASS. Full `perf_check.sh` run verified end to end.

**Why:** the plan doc said the 48 s cold start was "unreproduced by the committed script"; it is now reproduced, and the s5cmd retune (Q1) turned out unnecessary.
**How to apply:** for any perf branch, build via `build-perf.yml`, run `perf_check.sh` on the dev box, compare against the stored baseline. Images built after the `GIT_SHA` build arg landed label runs with the commit. See [[reference-gpu-server-ops]], [[project-cold-start-optimization]].
